# Iterating collections

## Default: for-each

```java
for (String name : names) System.out.println(name);
```

Works on any `Iterable`; compiles to an `Iterator` (`hasNext`/`next`).

## The trap: modify while iterating

```java
for (String n : names)
    if (n.isBlank()) names.remove(n);   // ConcurrentModificationException
```

Fails **fast** on structural change (single-threaded, despite the name). Fixes:

```java
names.removeIf(n -> n.isBlank());              // cleanest
for (var it = names.iterator(); it.hasNext();) // or remove via iterator
    if (it.next().isBlank()) it.remove();
```

Maps: `entrySet().removeIf(...)` / `values().removeIf(...)`.

## `forEach` & beyond

```java
names.forEach(System.out::println);
ages.forEach((name, age) -> ...);
```
